# Frontend Conventions

## Paths
- `@/*` → `client/`, `@shared/*` → `shared/` — prefer aliases over deep relatives

## Styling
- Tailwind 3 + tokens from `client/global.css` / `tailwind.config.ts`
- **Never** arbitrary colors (`text-emerald-500`, `bg-amber-400`, etc.)
- Use semantic tokens: `primary` (ink navy), `accent` (foundation gold), `destructive`, `muted`, `secondary`, `foreground`, `background`, `border`, `card`, `input`, `ring`
- Prefer existing `client/components/ui/` when present; Lucide icons first
- Brand logo: `/logos/groundwork-logo.png`

## Mobile responsiveness (mandatory on every UI change)
- Full standard: **`.cursor/rules/mobile-responsive.mdc`** (alwaysApply) — follow it on every `client/` change
- Design and verify for phones (~320–430px CSS px) and tablets — not desktop-only then “hope”
- **No document-level horizontal scrolling** (`html`/`body`/`#root` stay within viewport width; vertical-only page scroll)
- Prefer `minmax(0, 1fr)`, `width: 100%`, `max-width: 100%`, wrapping flex (`flex-wrap`), and single-column grids under ~760–900px
- Avoid fixed widths / large `min-width` that exceed the viewport; long text uses `overflow-wrap` / truncation inside cards
- Intentional sideways scroll (admin board columns, compact trackers, wide tables) MUST live inside a local `overflow-x: auto` wrapper with `max-width: 100%` — never leak to the page. Portal nav under 900px is an off-canvas drawer (not a chip strip).
- Touch targets: keep primary actions tappable; stack footer/header actions on small screens when needed
- **CSS cascade:** put responsive overrides **after** the base rules for the same selectors (or use mobile-first `min-width` queries). An early `@media (max-width: …)` block is overridden by later unscoped rules with equal specificity — that caused ADU options to stay 2-column on phones
- Before finishing a UI change: spot-check at **~320px and ~375px** for overflow (`scrollWidth <= clientWidth`), clipped CTAs, and unusable tables/forms/modals

## i18n (mandatory on every UI change)
- **Never hardcode** user-visible strings in components (including buttons, labels, empty states, errors, Yup messages, `aria-label`, PageMeta title/description)
- Add keys to **both** `client/locales/en/translation.json` and `client/locales/es/translation.json` in the same PR/change
- Use `t('namespace.key')` via `useTranslation()`
- Language detection: `localStorage` then `navigator`; **fallbackLng is `en`** (`client/i18n.ts`)
- Supported languages: `en`, `es` only
- Prefer split keys for emphasized copy (`titleBefore` / `titleEm` / `titleAfter`) over embedding HTML in JSON

## SEO
- Use **`PageMeta`** (`client/components/PageMeta.tsx`) on every route — do not hand-roll `Helmet` title/description/OG tags
- Pass i18n strings for `title` / `description` / `keywords`; set `noIndex` on unlisted flows

## Design docs (mandatory on UI/brand/email changes)
- **ALWAYS update `DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`** in the same change when visuals, branding, email chrome, public pages, or product flows change

## Forms
- Formik + Yup; reusable schemas; submit via Redux thunks
- Validation message strings must be i18n keys

## Logging
- UI: `client/utils/logger.ts` only (not raw `console.*`)
